  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "SDK 3.10.4 and earlier\n\nExecuting the following UdonSharp code yields the attached behavior:\n\n`Debug.Log($\"int -> long: {new DataToken(-1).Long}\");`\n\n`Debug.Log($\"uint -> long: {new DataToken(0u).Long}\");`\n\nThe first line prints `int -> long: 4294967295` instead of the expected text `int -> long: -1`. This implies DataToken is treating the 32-bit integral value as unsigned during the conversion instead of signed as is expected.\n\nThe second line throws an exception with the message `Attempted to access UInt token as Long` and does not print the expected text `uint -> long: 0`. This makes no sense, as the canonical widening conversion from uint to long is lossless.",
